00:27:41.926 --> 00:27:44.295
RELATIVE TO AAPI WOMEN'S EQUAL

00:27:44.362 --> 00:27:45.397
PAY DAY. SENATOR MINH. THANK

00:27:45.463 --> 00:27:47.632
YOU, MR. PRESIDENT. ON BEHALF OF

00:27:47.699 --> 00:27:48.833
THE ASIAN AMERICAN AND PACIFIC

00:27:48.900 --> 00:27:50.935
ISLANDER LEGISLATIVE CAUCUS, I

00:27:51.002 --> 00:27:52.070
AM PLEASED TO PRESENT SR 80,

00:27:52.137 --> 00:27:54.005
WHICH RECOGNIZES MAY 3RD, 2024

00:27:54.072 --> 00:27:57.409
AS AAPI WOMEN'S EQUAL PAY DAY.

00:27:57.475 --> 00:27:59.244
THIS DAY IS MEANT TO BRING

00:27:59.310 --> 00:28:00.745
AWARENESS TO THE PAY INEQUITIES

00:28:00.812 --> 00:28:02.080
FACED BY AAPI WOMEN COMPARED TO

00:28:02.147 --> 00:28:04.582
THEIR MALE AND WHITE

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:05.583
COUNTERPARTS. THE COMBINED

00:28:05.650 --> 00:28:07.919
AVERAGE INCOME OF AAPI WOMEN IS

00:28:07.986 --> 00:28:09.754
$0.80 FOR EVERY DOLLAR MADE BY

00:28:09.821 --> 00:28:11.222
WHITE MEN IN THE UNITED STATES.

00:28:11.289 --> 00:28:12.891
AND THERE'S AN EVEN GREATER

00:28:12.957 --> 00:28:14.726
DISPARITY IN CALIFORNIA, WHERE

00:28:14.793 --> 00:28:15.860
AAPI WOMEN MAKE $0.72 FOR EVERY

00:28:15.927 --> 00:28:17.862
DOLLAR MADE BY A WHITE MALE.

00:28:17.929 --> 00:28:18.930
THESE DISPARITIES ARE ACTUALLY

00:28:18.997 --> 00:28:21.032
MUCH WORSE THAN THEY SOUND,

00:28:21.099 --> 00:28:23.568
BECAUSE ON AVERAGE, AAPI WOMEN

00:28:23.635 --> 00:28:25.470
ARE 50% MORE LIKELY TO HAVE A

00:28:25.537 --> 00:28:26.471
BACHELOR'S DEGREE, OVER 200%

00:28:26.538 --> 00:28:28.907
MORE LIKELY TO HAVE A ADVANCED

00:28:28.973 --> 00:28:30.708
DEGREE, SUCH AS AN MBA OR LAW

00:28:30.775 --> 00:28:33.545
DEGREE OR MD. AND SO THIS IS A

00:28:33.611 --> 00:28:35.780
REAL, REAL HUGE GAP WE'RE

00:28:35.847 --> 00:28:37.615
FACING. THIS WAGE GAP IS ALSO

00:28:37.682 --> 00:28:40.351
MUCH MORE LARGE WHEN WE THINK

00:28:40.418 --> 00:28:42.620
ABOUT ETHNIC SUBGROUPS AND

00:28:42.687 --> 00:28:43.621
DISAGGREGATION OF THE DIFFERENT

00:28:43.688 --> 00:28:45.857
TYPES OF APIS OUT THERE, SUCH AS

00:28:45.924 --> 00:28:47.058
KOREAN AND MALAYSIAN WOMEN, WHO

00:28:47.125 --> 00:28:48.927
EARN, ON AVERAGE, $0.77 ON THE

00:28:48.993 --> 00:28:50.061
DOLLAR. INDONESIAN, CAMBODIAN

00:28:50.128 --> 00:28:54.432
AND LAOTIAN WOMEN WHO EARN AN

00:28:54.499 --> 00:28:55.433
AVERAGE $0.64. TONGAN AND

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:57.569
BHUTANESE WOMEN WHO EARN ON

00:28:57.635 --> 00:28:58.636
AVERAGE $0.52, AND NEPALESE AND

00:28:58.703 --> 00:29:01.239
BANGLADESHI WOMEN WHO EARN ON

00:29:01.306 --> 00:29:03.108
AVERAGE $0.48 ON THE DOLLAR. IN

00:29:03.174 --> 00:29:05.210
THE UNITED STATES, MANY OF THESE

00:29:05.276 --> 00:29:06.344
WOMEN REPRESENT A SUBSTANTIAL

00:29:06.411 --> 00:29:07.879
PROPORTION OF FRONTLINE

00:29:07.946 --> 00:29:10.982
ESSENTIAL CARE WORKERS, WITH 27%

00:29:11.049 --> 00:29:12.150
OF THEM BEING CLASSIFIED AS

00:29:12.217 --> 00:29:14.285
ESSENTIAL WORKERS. WE NEED TO

00:29:14.352 --> 00:29:16.154
SUPPORT THE AAPI WOMEN WHO HELP

00:29:16.221 --> 00:29:17.555
KEEP CALIFORNIA'S ECONOMY MOVING

00:29:17.622 --> 00:29:18.656
FORWARD, AND BY RECOGNIZING AAPI

00:29:18.723 --> 00:29:20.892
WOMEN'S EQUAL PAY DAY, WE CAN

00:29:20.959 --> 00:29:22.060
HOPEFULLY BEGIN TO MAKE PROGRESS

00:29:22.127 --> 00:29:24.496
TOWARDS EQUALIZING THAT PAY GAP

00:29:24.562 --> 00:29:25.730
AND ACKNOWLEDGING THE PROFOUND

00:29:25.797 --> 00:29:27.332
ROLE THAT THESE WOMEN PLAY IN

00:29:27.398 --> 00:29:29.200
THE WORKFORCE. WE RESPECTFULLY

00:29:29.267 --> 00:29:31.069
ASK FOR AN AYE VOTE ON SR 80.

00:29:31.136 --> 00:29:31.736
THANK YOU, SENATOR MINH. SENATOR

00:29:31.803 --> 00:29:34.939
WAHAB, THANK YOU. I RISE ON

00:29:35.006 --> 00:29:36.774
BEHALF OF THE WOMEN'S CAUCUS AS

00:29:36.841 --> 00:29:38.343
WELL AS THE AAPI CAUCUS, AND I

00:29:38.409 --> 00:29:41.513
DO JUST WANT TO HIGHLIGHT THAT

00:29:41.579 --> 00:29:42.680
WE ARE TALKING ABOUT EQUAL PAY

00:29:42.747 --> 00:29:44.516
FOR EQUAL WORK. AND WHEN WE'RE

00:29:44.582 --> 00:29:46.151
TALKING ABOUT AAPI WOMEN AND

00:29:46.217 --> 00:29:48.052
YES, THEY ARE PAID ACTUALLY

00:29:48.119 --> 00:29:49.154
HIGHER THAN ANY OTHER WOMAN

00:29:49.220 --> 00:29:51.756
DEMOGRAPHIC IN THE WORKFORCE.

00:29:51.823 --> 00:29:52.824
AND THAT'S STILL A PROBLEM. AND

00:29:52.891 --> 00:29:54.726
WE'RE CONSISTENTLY FIGHTING

00:29:54.792 --> 00:29:56.361
FORWARD. BUT I ALSO WANT TO

00:29:56.427 --> 00:29:58.963
HIGHLIGHT WHEN PEOPLE COME TO

00:29:59.030 --> 00:30:00.131
THIS COUNTRY, THEY DO COME HERE

00:30:00.198 --> 00:30:01.799
FOR THE AMERICAN DREAM AND PART

00:30:01.866 --> 00:30:03.635
OF THAT AMERICAN DREAM. AND I'VE

00:30:03.701 --> 00:30:04.903
OFTEN SAID IT IS OBVIOUSLY HOME

00:30:04.969 --> 00:30:05.436
OWNERSHIP, BUT IT'S ALSO

00:30:05.503 --> 00:30:06.504
ECONOMIC PROSPERITY FOR THEIR

00:30:06.571 --> 00:30:08.907
FAMILIES. THE CONCERN THAT I SEE

00:30:08.973 --> 00:30:10.875
HERE IS THE FACT THAT, AGAIN, WE

00:30:10.942 --> 00:30:11.976
STILL CONTINUOUSLY TALK ABOUT

00:30:12.043 --> 00:30:15.113
DISCRIMINATION. WE STILL SEE

00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:16.114
OPEN SYSTEMIC DISCRIMINATION AND

00:30:16.181 --> 00:30:18.516
THE FACT THAT WOMEN ARE PAID

00:30:18.583 --> 00:30:20.351
LESS TO EVERY SINGLE DOLLAR A

00:30:20.418 --> 00:30:23.087
MAN EARNS IS STILL VERY MUCH

00:30:23.154 --> 00:30:24.088
PROBLEMATIC. AND IT'S EVEN

00:30:24.155 --> 00:30:25.890
HARDER FOR CERTAIN SUBGROUPS. AS

00:30:25.957 --> 00:30:28.893
MY COLLEAGUE STATED, MANY PEOPLE

00:30:28.960 --> 00:30:29.894
, ESPECIALLY IMMIGRANT WOMEN WHO

00:30:29.961 --> 00:30:31.062
COME TO THIS COUNTRY, DON'T ALL

00:30:31.129 --> 00:30:32.297
COME ON A LEVEL PLAYING FIELD.

00:30:32.363 --> 00:30:33.298
THERE ARE SOME WOMEN THAT COME

00:30:33.364 --> 00:30:35.433
HERE WITH GREEN CARDS AND STATUS

00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:36.534
AND THE SUPPORT OF THEIR

00:30:36.601 --> 00:30:38.703
GOVERNMENTS AS WELL AS

00:30:38.770 --> 00:30:39.804
BUSINESSES AND MUCH MORE. AND

00:30:39.871 --> 00:30:41.573
THERE ARE SOME FOLKS THAT COME

00:30:41.639 --> 00:30:42.707
HERE AS REFUGEES, ASYLUM SEEKERS

00:30:42.774 --> 00:30:45.310
OR COMPLETELY UNDOCUMENTED IN

00:30:45.376 --> 00:30:46.444
ANY WAY. THOSE INDIVIDUALS

00:30:46.511 --> 00:30:49.147
STRUGGLE WITH LANGUAGE BARRIERS,

00:30:49.214 --> 00:30:50.281
MAKING SURE THAT THEIR FAMILIES

00:30:50.348 --> 00:30:51.983
ARE TAKEN CARE OF, MAKING SURE

00:30:52.050 --> 00:30:53.384
THAT THEY HAVE A ROOF OVER THEIR

00:30:53.451 --> 00:30:54.519
HEAD, AND MUCH MORE. AND YET

00:30:54.586 --> 00:30:56.387
THEY STILL DO NOT GET PAID

00:30:56.454 --> 00:30:59.257
EQUALLY. AND THIS IS MODERN DAY

00:30:59.324 --> 00:31:02.327
SLAVERY. WE TALK ABOUT IT IN THE

00:31:02.393 --> 00:31:03.461
LABOR MOVEMENT WITH WAGE THEFT.

00:31:03.528 --> 00:31:06.030
WE TALK ABOUT IT IN REGARDS TO A

00:31:06.097 --> 00:31:07.999
NUMBER OF OTHER WAYS, AND YET WE

00:31:08.066 --> 00:31:10.301
STILL CONTINUE TO SEE PEOPLE

00:31:10.368 --> 00:31:11.402
TAKE ADVANTAGE OF THE MOST

00:31:11.469 --> 00:31:13.271
